      "material": true,
      "rationale": "Exact local bytes, deterministic tests, package identities, and accepted structural evidence support the scoped self-consistency claim, while semantic independence, measured learning value, controller enforcement, and release lifecycle outcomes remain separate unobserved gates.",
      "statement": "On this Windows host, analyze-project-claims applied its own accepted component-map and evidence-bound protocol to the local v0.9.0 candidate. The exact accepted map passed an unchanged reconciliation and preflight; the package, embedded engine, and official skill validator verified; 250 of 251 repository tests passed with one privilege-dependent symlink skip; and fifteen focused tests validated the closed digest-bound evaluation manifest/result contract, exact fixture and repetition binding, recomputed gates, direct-failure precedence, and state-free validation. This establishes local structural self-consistency only: no representative pilot, pinned model evaluation, quality improvement, independent implementation, trusted repair controller, release, installation, or activation was observed.",
      "status": "partially_supported"
    }
  ],
